---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import SelectionSlotDemo from '../../components/SelectionSlotDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Selection Slot"
  description="Swaps a toolbar for a selection toolbar in the same place, without moving the page."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Selection Slot</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows your normal tools until something is selected. Then it shows the selection toolbar in the same place. The row
    keeps its height, so nothing below it moves.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <SelectionSlotDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Selection Slot usage"
      code={`import { SelectionSlot } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/selection-slot";

<SelectionSlot
  active={selected.length > 0}
  selection={
    <div role="toolbar" aria-label="Selected items" className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <p role="status" className="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate">{selected.length} selected</p>
      <Button variant="outline" size="sm">Move</Button>
      <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" aria-label="Clear selection" onClick={clear}>
        Clear
      </Button>
    </div>
  }
>
  <FilterBar />
</SelectionSlot>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>active</code> chooses what shows. <code>children</code> are the tools for no selection, such as search and
      filters. <code>selection</code>
      is the toolbar for selected items. Other props, such as
      <code>className</code> and <code>ref</code>, go to the outer
      <code>div</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are no variants or sizes. The slot has no padding, border, or color. Its content sets the look, so it fits
      any toolbar.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Optional selection</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Selection only in the table layout"
      code={`const selection = layout === "table" && rows.length > 0
  ? <BulkRecordActions records={rows} clear={clear} />
  : undefined;

<div className="min-w-0 flex-1">
  <SelectionSlot active={!!selection} selection={selection}>
    <fieldset disabled={editing} aria-label="Table tools">…</fieldset>
  </SelectionSlot>
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>selection</code> can be <code>undefined</code> while
      <code>active</code> is false. Put the slot in a <code>min-w-0 flex-1</code>
      wrapper when it shares a row with other controls. A disabled
      <code>fieldset</code> in the tools still works, and so do disabled or busy buttons in the selection.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Fit the width</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      title="Fold actions into a menu in narrow slots"
      code={`.selected-wide { display: none; }

@container sprout-selection (width >= 36rem) {
  .selected-wide { display: flex; }
  .selected-menu { display: none; }
}

/* Tailwind: hidden @xl/sprout-selection:flex */`}
    />
    <p>
      The slot is a size container named <code>sprout-selection</code>. Use it to show buttons when the slot is wide and
      a "Selected actions" menu when it is narrow. The examples above switch at 36rem for tables and 44rem for files.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Focus</h2>
    <p>
      When the selection opens, the slot remembers the focused element. If focus was in the tools, which are now hidden,
      it moves to the first control in the selection. If focus was somewhere else, such as a row checkbox, it stays
      there.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the selection closes and its focused button goes away, focus goes back to the remembered element, if it is
      still on the page. Clear returns you to the checkbox or button you started from.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The hidden tools stay mounted, so their state survives. They are
      <code>inert</code> and <code>aria-hidden</code>, so Tab, clicks, and screen readers skip them. Give the selection
      a role and name, such as
      <code>role="toolbar"</code> with <code>aria-label="Selected items"</code>, and put the count in{' '}
      <code>role="status"</code> so it is announced. Give an icon-only or short button, such as Clear, an
      <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The selection fades in over 180ms. The tools hide at once, so the two never overlap. The fade stops when reduced
      motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The slot has no color of its own. The fade uses
      <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code> and <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
